-- title:
--   Constant-field change for polar differentials on X_{H'}(M/p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $H'$ be the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` attached to $(M/p) \mid M$, so that $\Gamma' =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) is the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image of the preimage of $H'$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M/p) \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, $\gamma \mapsto d \bmod (M/p)$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $K$ an algebraically closed field that is a $k$-algebra. For a field $L$, write $F_L =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC L Γ'` for the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the ratios $\iota_L(p_f)/\iota_L(p_g)$, where $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ are integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms $f, g$ of one weight on $\Gamma'$ and the image $\iota_L(p_g)$ of $p_g$ in $L((q))$ is nonzero. The assertion is that there exists a $K$-linear map $\Phi : K \otimes_k \Omega_{F_k/k} \to \Omega_{F_K/K}$ which (i) is injective, (ii) satisfies $\Phi(c \otimes f\,\mathrm{d}g) = c\,(f'\,\mathrm{d}g')$ for all $c \in K$, $f, g \in F_k$ and $f', g' \in F_K$ whose Laurent series are obtained from those of $f$, resp. $g$, by applying $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,k\,K$ to all coefficients, and (iii) maps the base change to $K$ of `ssPolarDifferentials k Γ' p` onto `ssPolarDifferentials K Γ' p`; here, for a field $L$, `ssPolarDifferentials L Γ' p` is the $L$-submodule of $\Omega_{F_L/L}$ consisting of those $\omega$ that are regular at every place of $F_L$ over $L$ outside the set `ssPlacesQExp L Γ' p` of places satisfying the predicate `IsSSPlaceQExp L Γ' p`, and have a simple pole at every place in that set.
--
--   This is the constant-field extension statement for the component through $\infty$ of the mod $p$ fibre of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H'}(M/p)$: extension of an algebraically closed base field of characteristic $p$ identifies $K \otimes_k$ (differentials regular outside the distinguished places, with at most simple poles there) with the corresponding space over $K$. It is used in the construction of the maps relating these polar differentials to the multiplicative part of the Tate module and to torsion of the relevant Jacobian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_linearMap_injective_tensorProduct_kaehler_map_ssPolarDifferentials_eq.lean

